sentences.l:
“Ah, truly now the gods have called me to death;
for Deiphobus the hero I thought to be present,
but he is inside the wall, and me Athena has deceived.

who goes to the plain through the murky clouds
to snatch either a tender lamb or a cowering hare;
so Hector swooped, swinging his sharp sword.

foolish one; but away from him a far better helper
by the hollow ships I was left behind,
I who loosened your knees;

He spoke, and from the corpse drew out his bronze spear,
and laid it aside, and from the shoulders was stripping the armour,
blood-stained;

There lies by the ships a dead man, unwept, unburied,
Patroclus; and him I will not forget, so long as I
am among the living and my own knees move;

Of both feet behind he pierced both tendons
to the ankle from the heel, and attached oxhide straps,
and bound them to the chariot, and let the head drag;

And from him as he was dragged there was a cloud of dust, and around
dark hair streamed out, and the head, all of it, in the dust
lay, formerly graceful;
